    <bpmn:process id="W_W1914" name="W1914. Industry Trend &amp; Macro-Economic Impact Analysis" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly economic review; major macro event
Frequency: Quarterly analysis; ad-hoc for major events
Volume: Philippine economic indicators relevant to home improvement retail
Owner: FP&amp;A
Participants: FP&amp;A, VP Merchandising, CFO
Source: workflow W1914 — Industry Trend &amp; Macro-Economic Impact Analysis</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1914_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1914_Lane1" name="FP&amp;A">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1914_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1914_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1914_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1914_Lane2" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1914_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1914_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1914_Start4" name="Quarterly economic review; major macro event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1914_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1914_Task5" name="FP&amp;A monitors macro-economic indicators: (a) GDP growth rate (PSA) —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: FP&amp;A monitors macro-economic indicators: (a) GDP growth rate (PSA) — construction sector GDP specifically, (b) inflation rate (PSA CPI) — impact on consumer purchasing power and BuildRight&#x27;s cost structure, (c) interest rates (BSP policy rate) — impact on consumer financing (W38) and BuildRight&#x27;s borrowing costs, (d) exchange rate (PHP/USD, PHP/CNY) — impact on import costs (W2B), (e) OFW remittance growth (BSP) — key driver for Philippine home construction spending, (f) construction permits issued (PSA) — leading indicator for home improvement demand, (g) government infrastructure spending (DPWH) — drives contractor demand for BuildRight products, (h) typhoon frequency and severity (PAGASA) — drives demand for repair and reconstruction materials
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Ongoing (2–3 hours/week)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1914_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1914_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1914_Task6" name="Quarterly: FP&amp;A prepares economic impact assessment: (a) which economic trends…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly: FP&amp;A prepares economic impact assessment: (a) which economic trends will most impact BuildRight in the next 6–12 months?, (b) impact on sales: positive (e.g., strong construction growth → higher contractor demand) or negative (e.g., inflation reducing consumer DIY spending), (c) impact on costs: FX impact on imports, wage inflation, freight cost trends, (d) recommendations: adjust buying strategy, pricing, or expansion plans based on economic outlook
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1914_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1914_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1914_Task7" name="Annual: CFO incorporates economic outlook into strategic planning per W33: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Annual: CFO incorporates economic outlook into strategic planning per W33: (a) 3-year revenue forecast with economic scenarios (base, optimistic, pessimistic), (b) cost projection with FX and inflation assumptions, (c) capital allocation recommendations based on economic cycle positioning
Responsible (R): CFO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per W33</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1914_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1914_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1914_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1914_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-374 (ensure controlled execution — Market &amp; Competitive Intelligence (PA-44.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: FP&amp;A</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
