    <bpmn:process id="W_W1915" name="W1915. Trade Area Demographic Analysis &amp; Store Location Market Sizing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store site evaluation (W1652); annual store performance analysis
Frequency: Per new site evaluation (~10–15/year); annual refresh for existing stores
Volume: Per store location; 5–10 km trade area analysis
Owner: Market Research Analyst
Participants: Market Research Analyst, COO, FP&amp;A
Source: workflow W1915 — Trade Area Demographic Analysis &amp; Store Location Market Sizing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1915_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1915_Lane1" name="Market Research Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1915_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1915_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1915_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1915_Lane2" name="COO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1915_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1915_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1915_Start4" name="New store site evaluation (W1652); annual store performance analysis">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1915_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1915_Task5" name="For new store site: Market Research Analyst conducts trade area analysis: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: For new store site: Market Research Analyst conducts trade area analysis: (a) population within 5 km and 10 km radius (PSA census data + projected growth), (b) household income distribution: % of households in middle-income bracket (primary BuildRight customer), (c) housing characteristics: % of owner-occupied homes (homeowners = BuildRight customers), average home age (older homes = more renovation spending), (d) construction activity: building permits issued in the area (past 3 years trend), (e) competitor presence: distance to nearest CitiHardware, Wilcon, ACE, or independent hardware stores, (f) accessibility: road network, public transport, visibility from main road, (g) estimated addressable market: population × average home improvement spend per household × market share target
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–3 days/site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1915_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1915_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1915_Task6" name="For existing stores: annual trade area refresh: (a) update population and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: For existing stores: annual trade area refresh: (a) update population and income data (new census or PSA projections), (b) assess competitive changes: new competitor stores in trade area (W1912), (c) store sales vs. market potential: is the store capturing its fair share of the trade area?, (d) identify underperforming stores where market potential is higher than actual sales (opportunity for improvement)
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 day/store (rotated; ~50 stores/year)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1915_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1915_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1915_Task7" name="COO and FP&amp;A use trade area analysis for: (a) new store go/no-go decision per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: COO and FP&amp;A use trade area analysis for: (a) new store go/no-go decision per W1652, (b) store performance expectation setting, (c) store closure evaluation per W703 (is the trade area deteriorating?)
Responsible (R): COO / FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1915_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1915_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1915_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
