    <bpmn:process id="W_W1916" name="W1916. Supplier Market Intelligence &amp; Raw Material Price Trend Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly commodity price review; significant price movement alert
Frequency: Monthly review; ad-hoc for significant movements
Volume: Key commodities: steel, cement, copper, lumber, paint resins, plastic resins
Owner: Buyer
Participants: Buyer, Category Manager, FP&amp;A, VP Merchandising
Source: workflow W1916 — Supplier Market Intelligence &amp; Raw Material Price Trend Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1916_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1916_Lane1" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1916_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1916_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1916_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1916_Lane2" name="FP&amp;A">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1916_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1916_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1916_Start4" name="Monthly commodity price review; significant price movement alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1916_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1916_Task5" name="Buyer monitors key commodity prices: (a) steel rebar and flat steel (Philippine…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Buyer monitors key commodity prices: (a) steel rebar and flat steel (Philippine domestic price + China export price), (b) cement (Philippine domestic — Holcim, Republic, others), (c) copper wire (LME + import premium), (d) lumber (Philippine domestic + import), (e) paint raw materials (titanium dioxide, resins, solvents — global benchmark), (f) plastic resins (polypropylene, PVC — regional benchmark), (g) freight rates (container rates Shanghai-Manila)
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1916_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1916_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1916_Task6" name="Monthly: Buyer and Category Manager assess commodity impact: (a) which…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly: Buyer and Category Manager assess commodity impact: (a) which commodity prices have moved &gt; 5% in the past month?, (b) impact on BuildRight&#x27;s COGS: which categories are most affected?, (c) impact on vendor pricing: are vendors passing through cost increases? Are there opportunities to negotiate better terms when commodity prices decline?, (d) forward outlook: are prices expected to continue rising or declining?, (e) action: (i) if prices rising: accelerate purchases to buy before further increase, negotiate price holds with vendors, evaluate retail price increase per W40, (ii) if prices declining: delay purchases, negotiate vendor price reductions, consider promotional pricing to drive volume
Responsible (R): Buyer / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 day/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1916_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1916_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1916_Task7" name="Quarterly: FP&amp;A incorporates commodity price trends into cost forecast: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly: FP&amp;A incorporates commodity price trends into cost forecast: (a) projected COGS impact for next quarter, (b) margin impact and pricing action needed, (c) FX + commodity combined impact on import costs
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1916_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1916_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1916_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1916_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-374 (ensure controlled execution — Market &amp; Competitive Intelligence (PA-44.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Buyer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
